{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/432735-pacts-weighted-towards-the-mortal","id":432735,"title":"Pacts Weighted Towards the Mortal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-08T10:47:45-07:00","id":432735,"title":"Pacts Weighted Towards the Mortal","content":"There doesn't seem to be a drawback for just heaping your mortal with more and more stuff. Doesn't cost extra willpower. What's to stop a Demon from giving say his head cultist Resources 5 every time they renew their Pact for another year of dedicated service?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T11:55:08-07:00","id":432871,"title":"","content":"Predominantly the ST.<br /> <br /> Remember anything granted to your cult or members of it by contract don't benefit from merit sanctity. So if your ST decided that you were abusing the fact that the contract mechanics don't generally work towards preventing a demon from giving itself the short end of the stick, there is nothing stopping them from just having something take out the mortal or his resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-08-2015, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:07:31-07:00","id":432996,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ST discretion. Personally, I think it's great that the mechanics allow a Demon to grant hefty Merits, and it's even better if they do it to help themselves. A Demon should be able to raise their favorite cultist to the heights of wealth and fame, and then hang out on their guy's yacht for free. And that just gives the ST more mortal entanglements to play with. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if bums all over Seattle are suddenly winning the lottery, that's going to raise suspicions all over the place.<br /> <br /> The most problematic potential use of merit dots, I think, is using them to create your own occult experts and occult libraries out of nothing. &quot;So there's a werewolf in town? No problem, I find an unemployed librarian to pact with and give him a bunch of Merits and a new car, then ask him how to kill werewolves.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4832-dannyk","name":"DannyK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:38:21-07:00","id":433052,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human\">I remember this thread.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:50:23-07:00","id":433277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/432735-pacts-weighted-towards-the-mortal?p=433052#post433052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/259220-the-pacts-no-drawbacks-for-advantaging-the-human&quot;]I</a> remember this thread.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have done better when I attempted to search for this topic. If only I had your dots in Investigation (Forums).<br /> <br /> I knew somebody else must have had this question in the past two years.<br /> <br /> That having been said, thanks for directing me there Satchel. Thanks to nalak42 and DannyK for your responses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 03-08-2015, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T00:17:13-07:00","id":433640,"title":"","content":"In the mechanics of the system there is nothing to stop you heaping on the mortal.<br /> <br /> Except the mortal.<br /> <br /> The mortal has to have a reasonable chance of knowing what he is signing for and away. He doesn't have to believe it, he doesn't even have to be truly willing (he can be threatened into agreement) but he has to freely agree to it. Which means 9 times out of 10 unless you really swindle them with some good wording you don't actually have complete control over what you're giving the mortal. They will <i>want</i> things and if you give them extra then that's gravy. A washed up athlete isn't going to be interested in signing a pact to become your Cult Leader and occult librarian. He'll want his sporting career back. Remember: NPCs are supposed to be people and so have the same motivations as people.<br /> <br /> In short: Most people whom you pact with won't want anything to do with you. (Especially if it's a Soul Pact.) The ones whom you tailor are going to be effectively the Demonic equivalent to a vampire's ghoul. You'll have to groom them, make sure they're the one that you need, which means finding the right person, influencing that person subtly to your agenda, and finally making the deal. And that's all just to heap on the merits you want to exploit. Kinda more tricky than it immediately sounds, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:05:27-07:00","id":436432,"title":"","content":"Everyone here has given some great answers, so they mostly have it covered. I'd add only a couple things, really.<br /> <br /> For one, demons are not usually selfless humanitarians, giving away lots of bonuses for relatively little recompense. They do what they do in their best interests. Giving away a lot for little isn't much in your best interest, when you could be doing more or less the opposite. Could a charitable, kindhearted demon choose to give much and ask for little? Yes, but the World of Darkness and Unchained life will quickly prey upon those with good intentions.<br /> <br /> Another drawback is that it makes a <i>lot</i> of ripples. Giving away more and more pact-based benefits puts you right at the center of these ripples. The common link between people who are getting rich, or more influential, or gaining newfound strength, suddenly conquering disease, etc., is you. Most mortals might not know what it all means, but the right ones\u2014angels and the God-Machine, for example\u2014<i>will </i>know what to look for. Now you've attracted more attention than is healthy for a demon, and don't have much in the way of resources for all that you've given when the angels come knocking.<br /> <br /> Other demons might even see you as a prime target. If they can acquire your contracts, those mortals who have gotten so used to the wealth (in whatever form) you've granted them won't want to give it up. So now they're willing to pay much steeper prices, leaving you with nothing but a setup for other, more opportunistic demons to capitalize upon.<br /> <br /> In short, no, there is nothing in the rules stopping you from giving away lots of benefits for relatively little gain. In the setting, the consequences can be much more punishing than makes it worthwhile. No one ever said being a humanitarian in the World of Darkness was easy. That goes double for the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}